In `rebuild_utxos`, `utxo.is_trusted` is never set (defaults to `false`). In the live `update_utxos` path, `is_trusted` is set for change outputs of our own spend transactions (`has_owned_input && change_addrs.contains(&addr)`). After a rewind, formerly-confirmed self-spends become `Mempool`; because `utxo.is_confirmed` is also `false` (the context is no longer confirmed), `update_balance` places those UTXOs in the `unconfirmed` bucket rather than `confirmed`. The post-rewind balance will show less confirmed Dash than the wallet knows should be available, potentially causing the user to wait for confirmations on funds that should already be trusted. This is conservative (never over-states confirmed balance) but is a behavioral regression compared to the pre-reorg state. Restoring `is_trusted` during rebuild requires knowing which outputs are change addresses for the account, which the rebuild loop already has access to via `self.keys.managed_account_type().contains_address(&addr)` combined with the internal/change pool check.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

````suggestion
Within the output loop in `rebuild_utxos`, reconstruct the trusted-output flag:

```rust
// has_owned_input is true when any input of this tx spent a wallet UTXO
// (which spent_outpoints already tracks from earlier records in this rebuild).
let has_owned_input = tx.input.iter()
    .any(|i| self.spent_outpoints.contains(&i.previous_output));
// change_addr check requires access to the internal pool set; alternatively
// use the account type's internal-address predicate if one is exposed.
let is_change = self.keys.managed_account_type().is_internal_address(&addr);
utxo.is_trusted = has_owned_input && is_change;
```

Note: `is_internal_address` may not exist yet and would need to be added; the caveats are that (a) processing order still affects `spent_outpoints` at the point of the check (see blocker above — fix that first), and (b) mempool→mempool chains need topological order for `has_owned_input` to be accurate.
````
</details>

